    'Accept the public floor request and return a dict with areas, neighbors, and start. areas is a list of positive integer free-cell areas indexed by region. neighbors is a parallel list of lists of (neighbor_index, fee) pairs representing legal crossings in both directions. start is the index containing entry. Every region is internally connected by zero-fee moves, every free cell belongs to exactly one region, and crossing edges preserve the stated fees and legal reachability. Regions may represent many cells to support large coordinate extents. Preserve half-open blocked rectangles, additive fees for overlapping walls, and closed crossings for null fees.\n\nLocal check: Use a 3 by 1 free floor entered at (0, 0), place two walls of fees 2 and 3 on the first shared side, and a null-fee wall on the second side. Assert exactly three area-1 regions irrespective of indexing, one bidirectional connection of fee 5 from start, and no route edge to the isolated region.'
